2026-10-11 11:38:17,540 - RapidOCR - INFO: [[[[180.0, 100.0], [406.0, 100.0], [406.0, 123.0], [180.0, 123.0]], 'NeonatalResearchNetwork', 0.9979685078496519], [[[1249.0, 100.0], [1352.0, 100.0], [1352.0, 123.0], [1249.0, 123.0]], 'IND 142279', 0.990549647808075], [[[179.0, 129.0], [405.0, 129.0], [405.0, 155.0], [179.0, 155.0]], 'Budesonide in Babies (BiB)', 0.9729300897855025], [[[1229.0, 130.0], [1352.0, 130.0], [1352.0, 153.0], [1229.0, 153.0]], 'NCT04545866', 0.999779690395702], [[[178.0, 160.0], [377.0, 160.0], [377.0, 186.0], [178.0, 186.0]], 'Statistical Analysis Plan', 0.9983323526382446], [[[1192.0, 162.0], [1351.0, 162.0], [1351.0, 182.0], [1192.0, 182.0]], 'NICHD-NRN-0064', 0.9993772506713867], [[[179.0, 283.0], [841.0, 283.0], [841.0, 309.0], [179.0, 309.0]], '1BACKGROUNDANDPROTOCOL HISTORY', 0.9826525350411733], [[[179.0, 345.0], [1349.0, 345.0], [1349.0, 377.0], [179.0, 377.0]], 'Preterm birth is one of the leading causes of neonatal death worldwide (0.97 million, ~35% of all', 0.9976172797458688], [[[179.0, 382.0], [1345.0, 382.0], [1345.0, 411.0], [179.0, 411.0]], 'neonatal deaths), and approximately 1 in 8 births in the United States are preterm (Preterm Birth:', 0.9878554575297297], [[[179.0, 415.0], [1342.0, 415.0], [1342.0, 447.0], [179.0, 447.0]], 'Causes, Consequences, and Prevention, 2007). Bronchopulmonary dysplasia (BPD) is one of the', 0.9918210971486437], [[[176.0, 449.0], [1328.0, 448.0], [1328.0, 481.0], [176.0, 482.0]], 'most common morbidities in extremely preterm infants and is a competing outcome with death.', 0.9944784451317001], [[[178.0, 483.0], [1287.0, 482.0], [1287.0, 515.0], [178.0, 516.0]], 'BPD is associated with worse cognitive outcomes in school age children and with abnormal', 0.9951366551897742], [[[179.0, 519.0], [1293.0, 518.0], [1293.0, 548.0], [179.0, 549.0]], 'pulmonary function in adolescence and adulthood (Short et al., 2003; Halvorsen et al., 2004;', 0.9842986963365389], [[[179.0, 553.0], [1303.0, 553.0], [1303.0, 583.0], [179.0, 583.0]], 'Northway et al., 1990). Use of postnatal steroids to reduce BPD/death is generally minimized', 0.9839193445184956], [[[179.0, 587.0], [1316.0, 588.0], [1316.0, 618.0], [179.0, 617.0]], 'due to concerns of neurodevelopmental impairment. However, recent preliminary studies have', 0.998720641930898], [[[178.0, 620.0], [1345.0, 621.0], [1345.0, 654.0], [178.0, 653.0]], 'shown evidence that co-administered surfactant and glucocorticoid (budesonide) reduces the risk', 0.9952755777459396], [[[180.0, 658.0], [1278.0, 658.0], [1278.0, 687.0], [180.0, 687.0]], 'of BPD/death (Yeh et al., 2008; Yeh et al., 2016; Venkataraman et al., 2017; Hascoet et al.,', 0.9905640923458597], [[[181.0, 694.0], [1351.0, 694.0], [1351.0, 720.0], [181.0, 720.0]], '2018). Additional studies have shown that budesonide does not accumulate in the central nervous', 0.9742655465477391], [[[177.0, 789.0], [1267.0, 790.0], [1267.0, 820.0], [177.0, 819.0]], 'To further assess the safety and efficacy of co-administered surfactant and budesonide, the', 0.9903373888560704], [[[178.0, 824.0], [1338.0, 824.0], [1338.0, 856.0], [178.0, 856.0]], 'Neonatal Research Network (NRN) will conduct a large, multicenter clinical trial comparing the', 0.9984529811017057], [[[178.0, 855.0], [1306.0, 858.0], [1306.0, 891.0], [178.0, 888.0]], 'effects of combined surfactant and budesonide (intervention, 2.5 ml/kg surfactant + 1.0 ml/kg', 0.9933441819683198], [[[179.0, 893.0], [1315.0, 895.0], [1315.0, 924.0], [179.0, 922.0]], 'budesonide) versus surfactant alone (active control, 2.5 ml/kg surfactant) in extremely preterm', 0.9841261709991255], [[[178.0, 926.0], [1322.0, 927.0], [1322.0, 960.0], [178.0, 959.0]], 'babies (22 0/7 - 28 6/7 gestation age or birthweight <1000g). For consistency, all sites will use', 0.9880682236140537], [[[179.0, 960.0], [1335.0, 962.0], [1335.0, 995.0], [179.0, 993.0]], 'Curosurf as the surfactant and Pulmicort or generic budesonide for the budesonide. The primary', 0.9924158016417889], [[[179.0, 997.0], [1314.0, 999.0], [1314.0, 1029.0], [179.0, 1027.0]], 'outcome is a composite measure of physiologic BPD or death by 36 weeks post-menstrual age', 0.9913937878072931], [[[179.0, 1031.0], [1272.0, 1030.0], [1272.0, 1063.0], [179.0, 1064.0]], '(PMA), as these are competing outcomes. This will be a masked, randomized trial with 1:1', 0.9912814484401182], [[[178.0, 1066.0], [1246.0, 1067.0], [1246.0, 1097.0], [178.0, 1096.0]], 'treatment allocation. All 15 NRN centers plan to participate in the study; NRN study site', 0.9918212870533547], [[[180.0, 1102.0], [1207.0, 1101.0], [1207.0, 1131.0], [180.0, 1132.0]], '(hospital/NICU) will be incorporated into the randomization scheme and analyses via', 0.9905076357255499], [[[181.0, 1137.0], [647.0, 1137.0], [647.0, 1167.0], [181.0, 1167.0]], 'stratification and covariate adjustment.', 0.9906850457191467], [[[179.0, 1196.0], [460.0, 1201.0], [460.0, 1234.0], [178.0, 1229.0]], '1.1Protocol History', 0.997269514359926], [[[180.0, 1264.0], [1299.0, 1264.0], [1299.0, 1294.0], [180.0, 1294.0]], 'The first version of the statistical analysis plan (SAP, Version 1.0) was submitted to the FDA', 0.9851944338768086], [[[180.0, 1298.0], [1338.0, 1298.0], [1338.0, 1330.0], [180.0, 1330.0]], 'with a version of the protocol dated 15-MAY-2020. In subsequent versions of the SAP, protocol', 0.990554105850958], [[[180.0, 1333.0], [1329.0, 1332.0], [1329.0, 1362.0], [180.0, 1363.0]], 'changes that are relevant to the analysis will be summarized here. As of Version 1.2 of the SAP', 0.9910670612987719], [[[181.0, 1403.0], [966.0, 1403.0], [966.0, 1433.0], [181.0, 1433.0]], 'impact the prespecified statistical analyses described in this SAP.', 0.9980121690835526], [[[178.0, 1497.0], [643.0, 1497.0], [643.0, 1526.0], [178.0, 1526.0]], '2PURPOSE OF THE ANALYSIS', 0.963078091541926], [[[181.0, 1562.0], [1331.0, 1562.0], [1331.0, 1592.0], [181.0, 1592.0]], 'This statistical analysis plan (SAP) contains detailed information about statistical analyses to be', 0.9782160719235738], [[[179.0, 1596.0], [1304.0, 1597.0], [1304.0, 1627.0], [179.0, 1626.0]], 'performed to conduct statistical interim monitoring and assess the efficacy and safety of early', 0.9956600233128197], [[[179.0, 1628.0], [1323.0, 1632.0], [1323.0, 1662.0], [179.0, 1658.0]], 'intratracheal co-administration of surfactant and budesonide to extremely preterm infants using', 0.9889717045583223], [[[180.0, 1664.0], [1301.0, 1666.0], [1301.0, 1696.0], [180.0, 1694.0]], 'data from a randomized, masked, active-controlled clinical trial. The results of these analyses', 0.9945042283911454], [[[181.0, 1701.0], [1177.0, 1701.0], [1177.0, 1731.0], [181.0, 1731.0]], 'will be published in peer reviewed journals and presented at scientific conferences.', 0.9894559156327021], [[[180.0, 1836.0], [379.0, 1836.0], [379.0, 1862.0], [180.0, 1862.0]], 'Version 1.3,2024-09-10', 0.9950441474264319], [[[1294.0, 1836.0], [1354.0, 1836.0], [1354.0, 1865.0], [1294.0, 1865.0]], 'Page 1', 0.9604931473731995]]
